<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="recommended-gear">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c1" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ability_defend.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Recommended Gear for Protection Warriors in Mists of Pandaria Classic</span></h2>
<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="what-is-the-bis-protection-warrior-gear">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c1" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ability_warrior_revenge.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> What is the BiS Protection Warrior gear?</h3>
<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>The <span class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_warrior.gif");'></span>
<span class="c1">Protection Warrior</span> stat priority may seem simple in theory, but it is ever complicated by the different roles a <span class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_warrior.gif");'></span>
<span class="c1">Protection Warrior</span> can fulfill, and by the era of <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=84840/vengeance">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_charm.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vengeance</span></a>, the emphasis on damage output by tanks is increasing. Our quest for the <b>"best gear"</b> is not only complicated by trying to balance survivability and offensive utility, but also by the fact that we tend to excel in the off-tank position, meaning we should be able to easily swap to <span class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/role_dps.gif");'></span>Arms spec if only a single tank is needed for the encounter. Additionally, even if you were to prioritize full defense, your stat priority will change based on how you choose to utilize your active mitigation. <br/>
<br/>Everything from talents, to gear, to enchants belong on a spectrum between full beef-mode and full DPS-mode, and where each individual fall on that spectrum will be different depending on how comfortable you are with the class, what type of content you're aiming to do, along with how much trust you have in the rest of your raid. <b>
<i>It's unlikely that being towards either side of that spectrum will be the best thing for you and your raid group</i></b>, so make gearing adjustments that fit within the context of how you approach the game. <br/>
<br/>In this section, I will do my best to convey the gearing path you should go down if you're looking to take a <i>balanced</i> gearing approach.<br/>
<br/>I recommend familiarizing yourself with the <a data-contiguous="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/guide/classes/warrior/protection/tank-stat-priority-pve">Protection Warrior Stat Priority</a> before considering your best in slot loot. Generally, we'll prefer gear that favors <b>Parry</b> and <b>Dodge</b>, but different encounters will call for different gear. While raid drops are generally the most reliable way of getting high item level gear, many other items can be just as good, if not better.<ul class="exclude-units"></ul>
<br/>
<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="bis-gear">Overall Best in Slot Gear for Protection Warriors</h3>Raids releases in Mists of Pandaria Classic will be staggered, with a few resets between each raid opening. This means that as the Phase progresses, more of your Best in Slot gear will become available to you. This also means that you will need to find alternatives until your Best in Slot items are available. Below we have included three gear planners, corresponding with each raid release.<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
