<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="set-bonuses">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c1" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_misc_treasurechest02b.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Tier &amp; Set Bonuses for Protection Warriors in Mists of Pandaria Classic</span></h2>The set bonuses for <span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" data-contiguous="true" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_warrior.gif");'></span>
<span class="c1">Protection Warriors</span> in Phase 1 are quite lackluster, and even in a full BIS set, you generally don't use the 4-set bonus. The 1-minute reduction of <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=12975/last-stand">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_ashestoashes.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Last Stand</span></a> is a solid bonus as it allows us to more frequently cover moments of vulnerability. Because the Helmet and Chest slots have our preferred stats, including at least these two pieces should be a no-brainer. <br/>
<br/>The 4-set may seem good on paper, but it offers limited utility in actuality, while having suboptimal stats. 5% increased absorption on <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=112048/shield-barrier">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_shield_07.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Shield Barrier</span></a> is not nothing, but very inconsequential. We don't use <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=2565/shield-block">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_defend.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Shield Block</span></a> for the rage cost reduction to have any real effect, but it can be a nice quality-of-life on fights like <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/npc=60999/sha-of-fear">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Sha of Fear</span></a>.<br/>
<br/>The DPS Tier is also worth giving a look over for a more offensive set. While the 2-set bonus does nothing, the 4-set cuts the cooldown of <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=1719/recklessness">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_criticalstrike.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Recklessness</span></a> in half.<h3 class="heading-size-3 heading-bar" id="tier-14-tank">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">Tier 14 (Tank) - <a data-entity="item-set" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item-set=1145/plate-of-resounding-rings">
