<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="hit-expertise">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c1" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ability_marksmanship.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Reaching Hit and Expertise Cap for Protection Warrior</span></h2>In Mists of Pandaria, your Hit cap is 7.5% Hit and 15% Expertise. Keep in mind that some abilities, such as the <span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" data-contiguous="true" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/race_draenei_female.gif");'></span> Draenei Racial Heroic Presence, will contribute to your overall Hit and/<wbr/>or Expertise needed.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="hit-rating">Hit Rating</h4>At 7.5% Hit, your attacks will no longer be able to miss Raid bosses. We prioritize Hit in our gearing, as even though it scales linearly to Expertise, some abilities, like <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=6343/thunder-clap">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_thunderclap.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Thunder Clap</span></a>, can miss but can't be dodged or parried.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="expertise-rating">Expertise Rating</h4>Expertise was changed to no longer grant reduction to <i>both</i> the target's ability to dodge <i>and</i> parry. When reaching 7.5% Expertise, you will have removed the boss's chance to dodge, but their chance to parry remains unchanged. You'll need an additional 7.5% Expertise to eliminate their chance to parry (15% total). <br/>
<br/>This means that while tanking a target, there is effectively no "soft cap" where Expertise starts dropping off in value. However, as you're not always dealing damage to a target head-on, it's still worth thinking about Expertise in terms of soft cap and hard cap. It's worth noting that if Shield Slam and Revenge is dodged or parried, they grant no Rage.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="gemming">
